# Applies to any image built with the repo root as context — the Cloud Run
# image (/Dockerfile) and docker/Dockerfile.prod.
# backend/.dockerignore and frontend/.dockerignore cover their own
# subdirectory-context builds (backend/Dockerfile, frontend/Dockerfile) and
# are unaffected by this file.

node_modules
**/node_modules
npm-debug.log*

# Build output. The Cloud Run image builds the SPA itself in its first stage;
# shipping a stale local dist/ into the context would be uploaded, ignored, and
# occasionally confusing.
frontend/dist/
dist/

# Translation working set — 337 files of machine-translated JSON that nothing
# at runtime reads. Locale tables ship from frontend/src/i18n/locales.
frontend/i18n-export/

# Local agent session state.
.codewhale/

# backend/.env is DELIBERATELY shipped in the image.
#
# Deliberate owner decision for this single-tenant, private repo: baking the
# file in means a Cloud Run revision boots with SMTP, AI and app config already
# populated instead of 40-odd env vars being re-entered in the console. The
# root .env stays excluded — it is compose-only and its values are wrong inside
# a container.
#
# What this costs, so it is a known trade and not a surprise later:
#   - `docker history` / any pull from Artifact Registry exposes the file, so
#     registry pull access == credential access. Keep the registry private.
#   - Rotating a key means rebuilding the image, not just editing a setting.
#
# dotenv does NOT override variables already in the environment, so anything
# set on the Cloud Run service still wins over this file. DATABASE_URL must be
# overridden there — the value here points at localhost:5433 and cannot resolve
# in Cloud Run.
.env
!backend/.env
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea

# Docs, local scratch, and anything Docker never needs to see.
*.md
backups/
tmp-server.log
tmp_shell_runner/
test-results/
e2e/
